    {
      "id": 23,
      "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC297229/",
      "title": "Brody JS, Stemmler EJ, DuBois AB. J Clin Invest 1968;47(4):783-799. doi:10.1172/JCI105773",
      "accessed": "2026-11-02",
      "source_id": "ONTO-RES:PMC297229",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "text": "The pulmonary arteries were responsible for 46% of total lobar vascular resistance, whereas the pulmonary capillaries and veins accounted for 34 and 20% of total lobar vascular resistance respectively.",
          "added": "2026-11-02"
        },
        {
          "text": "The pulmonary arteries accounted for approximately 50% of vascular resistance upstream from the sluice point when alveolar pressure exceeded venous pressure.",
          "added": "2026-11-02"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6039797/",
      "title": "Chamarthy MR, Kalva SP. Cardiovasc Diagn Ther 2018;8(3):208-213. doi:10.21037/cdt.2018.01.08",
      "accessed": "2026-11-02",
      "source_id": "ONTO-RES:PMC6039797",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "text": "Distribution of resistance Equal across arteries, capillaries and veins Predominantly muscular arterioles",
          "added": "2026-11-02"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 25,
      "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10110735/",
      "title": "Balistrieri A, ..., Yuan JX-J. Physiol Rev 2023;103(3):1827-1897. doi:10.1152/physrev.00030.2021",
      "accessed": "2026-11-02",
      "source_id": "ONTO-RES:PMC10110735",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "text": "In the systemic circulatory system, the muscular small arteries and arterioles (or resistance arteries) account for 70% of the pressure drop.",
          "added": "2026-11-02"
        },
        {
          "text": "The systemic capillaries and veins only account for 7% and 19% of the pressure drop, respectively",
          "added": "2026-11-02"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the pulmonary circulation system, however, the pressure drop is evenly distributed among the pulmonary arteries and veins.",
          "added": "2026-11-02"
        },
        {
          "text": "the pulmonary artery accounts for 30 ± 7% of the total pressure drop, whereas the pressure drop in the capillary and vein accounts for 17 ± 3% and 39 ± 13%, respectively.",
          "added": "2026-11-02"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 26,
      "url": "https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/efetch.fcgi?db=pubmed&id=3946629&retmode=xml",
      "title": "Davis MJ, Ferrer PN, Gore RW. Am J Physiol 1986;250(2 Pt 2):H291-H303 (hamster cheek pouch)",
      "accessed": "2026-11-02",
      "source_id": "ONTO-RES:PMID3946629",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "text": "Fifty percent of the total pressure drop across the cheek pouch vasculature occurs in the small cheek pouch arteries",
          "added": "2026-11-02"
        }
      ]
    }
